Store") -- including but not limited to Apple's App Store -- and to accept
that platform's standard terms for doing so, notwithstanding that those
terms may be inconsistent with sections 3, 4, 5, 6, 10 or 12 of the GNU
General Public License.

Without limiting the generality of the grant above, this permission
specifically covers:

 a) limits the platform imposes on the number or kind of devices on which a
    recipient may install the object code, and restrictions the platform
    imposes on a recipient's ability to redistribute object code obtained
    from it;

 b) digital rights management, code signing, or other technological
    measures applied to the object code by the platform or its operator,
    and any resulting inability of a recipient to install a modified
    version on a device;

 c) the absence of Installation Information, within the meaning of section
    6 of the License, for object code conveyed through such a platform;

 d) the platform operator conveying the object code to recipients under the
    platform's own end-user licence terms rather than under this License.

LIMITS OF THE GRANT

This permission extends only to conveying the work in object-code form
through such a platform. In particular:

 1) It grants nothing with respect to the Corresponding Source, which must
    still be offered under the terms of the GNU General Public License. A
    recipient who obtains the object code from an App Store remains
    entitled to the Corresponding Source on the ordinary terms of section
