 2) It does not permit linking or combining this work with software whose
    source is not available under a licence compatible with the GNU General
    Public License. A proprietary library is not made permissible by this
    exception merely because the platform that distributes the result is.

 3) It does not restrict any recipient who obtains the source, or an
    object-code build, by any other means. Such a recipient has the full
    rights the GNU General Public License grants, unmodified.

As provided by section 7 of the License, a recipient may remove this
additional permission from any copy of the work, or from any part of it,
that the recipient conveys.

If you modify this work, you may extend this permission to your modified
